# Repo-wide ignores. A folder's own .gitignore protects only that folder, and
# a folder that isn't tracked at all has nowhere to put one — which is how
# matching/.env sat in every working tree both untracked and unignored while
# holding a live API key (issue #89). Secrets are ignored from the root so a
# new top-level folder starts protected instead of having to remember.
#
# This deliberately does not ignore matching/ itself: that is source code
# living on feat/matching-engine, and ignoring the directory here would
# quietly stop it from ever being added. Ignoring the key is the point.

# --- secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# .env and .env.anything, except the committed example. frontend/.env.example
# is tracked, so the negation below is what keeps it addable.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- dependencies and build output -----------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
out/

# --- editor and OS noise ---------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log

# --- per-person tool settings ----------------------------------------------
# .claude/launch.json and settings.json are shareable, so the directory is
# left visible; settings.local.json is one person's own permission grants.
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- deploy tooling --------------------------------------------------------
# Written by `vercel link`; holds the project and org ids.
.vercel
